From: LuneOS <webos-ports@googlegroups.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] neva mime: keep WebM, Ogg and AAC when decoding in software

NevaMimeUtil::RemoveUnsupportedMediaFormats() dropped audio/webm, video/webm,
video/ogg, audio/aac and audio/x-m4a from the supported-container table for every
webOS build. On a TV that is correct -- decoding is done by fixed-function
hardware that cannot handle them, so advertising support would accept media that
then fails to play. On LuneOS the pipeline is GStreamer decoding in software, and
every one of these has a decoder present: matroskademux, avdec_vp8, avdec_vp9,
avdec_opus, vorbisdec, oggdemux, theoradec, qtdemux and avdec_aac.

USE_GST_MEDIA already marks that distinction, so the removals are now conditional
on it. The two WebM entries additionally honour the enable_webm_audio_codecs and
enable_webm_video_codecs GN args, which already gate the MediaSource side in
media/filters/stream_parser_factory.cc; without this the two disagreed, since
those args never reached the canPlayType path at all.

Effect on LuneOS: canPlayType and MediaSource.isTypeSupported both start
answering for WebM (VP8, VP9, AV1, Vorbis, Opus), Ogg Theora, and AAC in its
audio/aac and audio/x-m4a spellings, instead of reporting nothing for media the
device can actually play.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/media/base/neva/webos/neva_mime_util_internal_webosose.cc
+++ b/src/media/base/neva/webos/neva_mime_util_internal_webosose.cc
@@ -28,14 +28,32 @@
   AddContainerWithCodecs("service/webos-photo-camera", webos_codecs);
 #endif  // defined(USE_NEVA_MEDIA_PLAYER_CAMERA)
 }
+// These containers were removed unconditionally, which is right for a TV: there the neva media
+// pipeline hands decoding to fixed-function hardware that cannot do them, so claiming support would
+// accept media that then fails to play. It is wrong wherever the pipeline decodes in software.
+//
+// USE_GST_MEDIA is exactly that distinction -- it is set when the GStreamer pipeline is in use, as on
+// LuneOS, where every one of these has a decoder present (matroskademux, avdec_vp8, avdec_vp9,
+// avdec_opus, vorbisdec, oggdemux, theoradec, qtdemux, avdec_aac). The WebM pair additionally honours
+// the enable_webm_*_codecs GN args, which already gate the MSE side in stream_parser_factory.cc, so
+// that the two paths cannot disagree about what is playable.
+//
+// This is what canPlayType answers from; the GN args alone do NOT reach it, which is why WebM stayed
+// unsupported even with enable_webm_video_codecs=true.
 void NevaMimeUtil::RemoveUnsupportedMediaFormats() {
+#if !defined(ENABLE_WEBM_AUDIO_CODECS)
   RemoveContainer("audio/webm");
+#endif
+#if !defined(ENABLE_WEBM_VIDEO_CODECS)
   RemoveContainer("video/webm");
+#endif
+#if !defined(USE_GST_MEDIA)
   RemoveContainer("video/ogg");
-#if BUILDFLAG(USE_PROPRIETARY_CODECS)
+#endif
+#if BUILDFLAG(USE_PROPRIETARY_CODECS) && !defined(USE_GST_MEDIA)
   RemoveContainer("audio/aac");
   RemoveContainer("audio/x-m4a");
-#endif  // BUILDFLAG(USE_PROPRIETARY_CODECS)
+#endif  // BUILDFLAG(USE_PROPRIETARY_CODECS) && !defined(USE_GST_MEDIA)
 }
 }  // namespace internal
 }  // namespace media
